From: Mesa Developers <mesa-dev@lists.freedesktop.org>
Subject: [PATCH] util/rust/meson: add build root dir to include directories of libutil_rust_bindgen_c

The static inline wrapper generated by rust.bindgen includes the header
file relative to where bindgen gets executed (the build root), rather
than relative to the directory of the generated wrapper C file.

When building out-of-tree (e.g., meson setup mesa _build), clang fails with:
fatal error: '../mesa/src/util/rust/util_bindgen.h' file not found
because the build root is not present in the include path of the static
library.

Add the build root to include_directories via fs.relative_to, matching
the existing fixes in rusticl, kraid, and nvk (!29275, !42189, !43941).
---
 src/util/rust/meson.build | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/util/rust/meson.build b/src/util/rust/meson.build
index 195f9a36e1b..3adfefb826d 100644
--- a/src/util/rust/meson.build
+++ b/src/util/rust/meson.build
@@ -54,7 +54,10 @@ _util_rust_bindgen = rust.bindgen(
 libutil_rust_bindgen_c = static_library(
   'util_rust_bindgen_c',
   _util_rust_bindgen[1],
-  include_directories : inc_util,
+  include_directories : [
+    inc_util,
+    fs.relative_to(meson.project_build_root(), meson.current_source_dir()),
+  ],
   dependencies : [
     idep_mesautil.partial_dependency(compile_args : true, includes : true,
                                      sources : true),
-- 
